{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873215-beasts-and-the-god-machine","id":873215,"title":"Beasts and the God Machine","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-24T12:17:40-07:00","id":873215,"title":"Beasts and the God Machine","content":"Do we know anything off hand about whether there are any interaction between the two, even indirectly? I know the other splats do (as summarized <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/God-Machine\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> ), and that Beasts at the very least know Demons are <i>terrifying and not kin</i>. Is there anything else I'm missing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10141-solaris","name":"Solaris","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10141_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-24T12:35:56-07:00","id":873225,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/863271-beasts-and-demons-together-why\">This thread</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/850242-beast-nature-and-morality?p=851890#post851890\">this post</a>. Those immediately come to my egotistical mind.<br /> <br /> Plenty of room for discussion though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T01:28:20-07:00","id":873596,"title":"","content":"Why not? Similar to mages, Beasts build their powers by exploring the hidden corners of the world, learning all the fears and nightmares that afflict humanity. And the God-Machine has its probes in all sorts of strange phenomena and weird situations. . . Assuming the God-Machine's representative survive long enough to make their pitch, there's all sorts of things they can offer a Beast. Unlimited funds, access to rare supernaturals, human flunkies . . . Is it really that hard to see a Beast running a G-M cult, or (knowingly) protecting Infrastructure? <br /> <br /> There's also short piece of flash fiction in the corebook, where a Beast was palling around with a demon. The Beast found the demon fascinating. Almost as fascinating as selling the demon out, and watching the God-Machine's mechanical angels drag him off . . .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T16:03:26-07:00","id":874085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873215-beasts-and-the-god-machine?p=873596#post873596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's also short piece of flash fiction in the corebook, where a Beast was palling around with a demon. The Beast found the demon fascinating. Almost as fascinating as selling the demon out, and watching the God-Machine's mechanical angels drag him off . . .</div> </div> </div> </div>What page in the Corebook is this? I have it and now I want to see it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10141-solaris","name":"Solaris","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10141_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T02:36:00-07:00","id":874367,"title":"","content":"My theory on how come the God-Machine and its creations don't count as kin is because they have no connection to the Astral Realms. As far as I can tell, pretty much everything is connected to the Astral. Supernatural groups probably each have their own realm branching off from some remote portion of the Anima Mundi. Spirits are family and I doubt they're directly connected to the human portion of the Astral Realms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T02:44:36-07:00","id":874369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenorath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873215-beasts-and-the-god-machine?p=874367#post874367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My theory on how come the God-Machine and its creations don't count as kin is because they have no connection to the Astral Realms. As far as I can tell, pretty much everything is connected to the Astral. Supernatural groups probably each have their own realm branching off from some remote portion of the Anima Mundi. Spirits are family and I doubt they're directly connected to the human portion of the Astral Realms.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about vampires though? What connection do they have? Prometheans too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T09:19:45-07:00","id":874600,"title":"","content":"I think Beasts have a connection to everything that is or was human. Prometheans kinda count. Spirits might, in that they are sometimes generated or fed by humans. But the God-Machine is clearly not human (nor are its Angels, loyal or Fallen, no matter how well they pretend at it).<br /> <br /> &lt;shrug&gt; Beast claiming Kinship to everything and its cousin <i>but</i> the G-M never made much sense to me, personally.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T10:32:29-07:00","id":874656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873215-beasts-and-the-god-machine?p=874600#post874600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Beasts have a connection to everything that is or was human. Prometheans kinda count. Spirits might, in that they are sometimes generated or fed by humans. But the God-Machine is clearly not human (nor are its Angels, loyal or Fallen, no matter how well they pretend at it).<br /> <br /> &lt;shrug&gt; Beast claiming Kinship to everything and its cousin <i>but</i> the G-M never made much sense to me, personally.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not every spirit correspond to anything resembling a human produced phenomenon. In fact, I'd argue, most don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T10:38:11-07:00","id":874665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873215-beasts-and-the-god-machine?p=874656#post874656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not every spirit correspond to anything resembling a human produced phenomenon. In fact, I'd argue, most don't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hence, &quot;might&quot;. I don't actually see much sense in how Beasts claim Kinship. I was just trying to identify what common things I could.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T11:54:08-07:00","id":874753,"title":"","content":"It might be that the mechanichal nature of the G-M is alien to the Begotten?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T12:05:36-07:00","id":874762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873215-beasts-and-the-god-machine?p=874753#post874753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might be that the mechanichal nature of the G-M is alien to the Begotten?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would that make a difference? People fear machines.<br /> <br /> Personally, I run it so that any creature or supernatural which was once human or has a significant mythology built around them can have Kinship. Thus, demons cannot benefit from Kinship because, in general, when someone says 'demon', you don't immediately think 'bio-mechanical horror constructed by a God-Machine. Same goes for angels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T12:30:50-07:00","id":874786,"title":"","content":"But Beasts can have Kinship with spirits, including those from the Inferno.<br /> The God Machine is an immanent mechanichal deity, that doesn't seem to have any semblance of life or emotion past or present, unlike even Prometheans. It's just a giant, malevolent, almost omnipotent household appliance that creepily popped up from nowhere someday, not a parent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T12:41:00-07:00","id":874798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873215-beasts-and-the-god-machine?p=874786#post874786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Beasts can have Kinship with spirits, including those from the Inferno.<br /> The God Machine is an immanent mechanichal deity, that doesn't seem to have any semblance of life or emotion past or present, unlike even Prometheans. It's just a giant, malevolent, almost omnipotent household appliance that creepily popped up from nowhere someday, not a parent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it and did It, though? Maybe the &quot;retroactively appeared out of nowhere&quot; is the best bet for a why, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T13:31:29-07:00","id":874833,"title":"","content":"Maybe near its beginning the Machine decided that the Begotten and their Kinship were more trouble than they were worth*, and so set up some Infrastructure to seal any ties it or its creations (even the Unchained) from the connective powers of the Dark Mother's Brood? Heck, you could even have a big plot about the characters finding out and hunting down this ancient occult matrix to tear it down and drag the G-M and other Aetheric things into the fold, kicking and screaming if need be. <br /> <br /> *Such as the fear that that the companionship they provide might make Angels more likely to Fall by introducing them to foreign thoughts or fighting to prevent them from being recycled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T14:11:14-07:00","id":874864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873215-beasts-and-the-god-machine?p=874833#post874833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe near its beginning the Machine decided that the Begotten and their Kinship were more trouble than they were worth*, and so set up some Infrastructure to seal any ties it or its creations (even the Unchained) from the connective powers of the Dark Mother's Brood? Heck, you could even have a big plot about the characters finding out and hunting down this ancient occult matrix to tear it down and drag the G-M and other Aetheric things into the fold, kicking and screaming if need be.<br /> <br /> *Such as the fear that that the companionship they provide might make Angels more likely to Fall by introducing them to foreign thoughts or fighting to prevent them from being recycled.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not a bad idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873215-beasts-and-the-god-machine?p=874369#post874369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What about vampires though? What connection do they have? Prometheans too.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I'm not saying it is true, humanity and the Divine Fire seem to have some sort of connection and there isn't any reason why Vampires couldn't have there own Astral space or be piggybacking off of the human one. The connection might just be too weak to manifest anything of note.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T14:18:21-07:00","id":874870,"title":"","content":"For me, the argument has always laid in the divinity of the Machine, demonstrated by a deeply metaphysical <i>apartness</i> from reality. It is not of this world, not anymore if ever it was.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T20:22:04-07:00","id":875191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873215-beasts-and-the-god-machine?p=874870#post874870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me, the argument has always laid in the divinity of the Machine, demonstrated by a deeply metaphysical <i>apartness</i> from reality. It is not of this world, not anymore if ever it was.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I definitely agree with this. I also wonder if it has to do with the legends and 'primal fears' that Beasts are. Vampires, Werewolves, Spirits and Prometheans all seem to stem out of that (hence the 'younger cousin' analogy). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873215-beasts-and-the-god-machine?p=874762#post874762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ... in general, when someone says 'demon', you don't immediately think 'bio-mechanical horror constructed by a God-Machine. Same goes for angels.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that this is one valid reason to why the 'fear' doesn't allow that 'link', but also because Angels by the definition of being extentions of a 'God' would be just as old if not possibly <i>older</i> than the origin of beasts. Seperate from the 'younger/older cousin' analogy. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10141-solaris","name":"Solaris","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10141_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T00:17:46-07:00","id":875391,"title":"","content":"In my head canon, the God-Machine is like D&amp;D's Mind Flayers, a force from the future trying to conquer the past to extend its supremacy to all of spacetime. Coincidentally, this also explains its lack of ties to the ancient Dark Mother.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T06:05:51-07:00","id":875541,"title":"","content":"I use the literal description of Oil and Water. Water occurs naturally, oil is artificial, and the two don't mix. Beasts can't bond with anything GMy because they are too close to pure &quot;water&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T07:34:35-07:00","id":875615,"title":"","content":"Except...oils occur naturally. Your body produces tons of the stuff to protect your skin and hair...<br /> <br /> All kinds of things are hydrophobic (like your skin).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T08:59:00-07:00","id":875701,"title":"","content":"Another analogy, the GM is a prosthesis that has been jammed into a wound. Infrastructure and its metaphysical nature acts as the anti-rejection medication. Beast as embodiments of nature cannot bond, like skin cannot grow on titanium limbs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T10:00:42-07:00","id":875738,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1630_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1630\" data-vbnamecard=\"1630\">Jacob</a>, you really have trouble with metaphors, don't you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T18:51:12-07:00","id":876180,"title":"","content":"Except, the metaphor was based on broken logic...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T22:04:23-07:00","id":876277,"title":"","content":"The Unchained and the Begotten are loosely similar in that they both have major chunks of their metaphysics devoted to sympathetic connections tied to relationships \u2014 it's part of the basis for Cover and pactwork, as well as pretty much everything to do with Kinship and the Primordial Pathways. They differ, however, on two fairly key points:<br /> <br /> 1. The void that gives the Begotten their Hunger and allows them to reflect their monstrous kin is an intrinsic part of their nature as cells in the greater superorganism of the Primordial Dream. Demons, however, approach the hollows they deal with in much the same way as their creator, shuffling metaphysical debt around and recalling impersonal codes to the secret laws of the universe. The emptiness that the Unchained pursue is something external to them that they seek to possess and inhabit; the Children's is an internal process that they attempt to modulate.<br /> <br /> 2. The bonds conferred by the heritage of the Dark Mother are universally supernatural and otherworldly. The God-Machine as a general entity is almost aggressively mundane, and its rogue processes pick up a trick of semiotics that only works on supernatural beings through their capacity to affect a pretense of mortality \u2014 a trick that notably doesn't work on Beasts at all. What's more, while the trajectory of Begotten fatalism tends to mean characters become conceptually related to monsters they relate to and stay close to monsters they don't find repellant, demons become more distinctive as their developing niche in the universe and/or the loss of coherent Cover causes their individual strangeness to warp their interface with reality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":".  Dropped word-fragment. 04-28-2016, 01:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-27T22:33:26-07:00","id":876292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873215-beasts-and-the-god-machine?p=876180#post876180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except, the metaphor was based on broken logic...</div> </div> </div> </div>Except, a metaphor need not be perfect to make it's point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T07:27:50-07:00","id":876612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873215-beasts-and-the-god-machine?p=876292#post876292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except, a metaphor need not be perfect to make it's point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aren't we trying to understand <i>why</i> Beasts and the God-Machine don't mesh? In that manner, isn't the <i>why</i> of oil and water what's important here? Which is the problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T07:44:06-07:00","id":876628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873215-beasts-and-the-god-machine?p=875738#post875738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1630_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1630\" data-vbnamecard=\"1630\">Jacob</a>, you really have trouble with metaphors, don't you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I find that metaphors frequently add very little to conversations when they aren't used precisely, like a laser. They frequently obfuscate more than they illuminate. Just flat out going with oil and water would have worked fine but somehow naturally occurring and artificiality got clustered in and suddenly I went from reading a relatively good metaphor (tier 1) to a piss poor analogy (tier 2). My advice is, if you're going to use metaphors then take some time and use them correctly.<br /> <br /> These are web forums after all. There should be something to be said for clear and concise prose. Save your metaphors for your fan-fictions. (But also, most of the people employing metaphors just aren't very good at it. Selection is a key aspect and poor metaphors aren't as helpful as some make them out to be (in many cases no metaphor is better).) And finally, mixed metaphors = bad metaphors.<br /> <br /> My work here is done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1630,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","user":"Jacob","date":". 04-28-2016, 10:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T07:45:19-07:00","id":876629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873215-beasts-and-the-god-machine?p=876612#post876612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Aren't we trying to understand <i>why</i> Beasts and the God-Machine don't mesh? In that manner, isn't the <i>why</i> of oil and water what's important here? Which is the problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, no, on two fronts.<br /> <br /> 1) I know why Beasts and the God-Machine don't mesh. I already gave my answer. Is it canon? Enough.<br /> <br /> 2) Nyx's point is made, if you read the whole of her point. Oil and Water might not have been the best icons, sure, but it gets the idea of what they're talking about across. as is often the point, it's the image and enough of the context that matters. I dunno what Jacob's whining about, because I can't read a thing he says, but I'm fairly sure it's a realm of minutia that's beyond the point you were to take away from the image and the initial context.<br /> <br /> Metaphors are not one-to-one affairs, and they shouldn't be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T08:04:07-07:00","id":876639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873215-beasts-and-the-god-machine?p=876629#post876629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Nyx's point is made, if you read the whole of her point. Oil and Water might not have been the best icons, sure, but it gets the idea of what they're talking about across. as is often the point, it's the image and enough of the context that matters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except, no, it doesn't seem to be. We already know that Beast and G-M don't mix. But <i>why</i> is that, when Beast claims <i>everything else</i> as Kin? Other than authorial fiat. The &quot;Unnatural vs Natural&quot; argument breaks down when you look at 1. if it supported that either side is more &quot;natural&quot; than the other, and 2. why is the G-M the exception when Prometheans are obviously created, Arisen were created, and Deviants are created?<br /> <br /> I'm honestly curious how Beasts can claim Kinship to everything under the sun and moon <i>except</i>, strangely, anything G-M related. Where is the unifying element that is absent there?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T09:29:13-07:00","id":876730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873215-beasts-and-the-god-machine?p=876639#post876639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But <i>why</i> is that, when Beast claims <i>everything else</i> as Kin? Other than authorial fiat.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The animal parts of the collective human consciousness&quot; and &quot;the emergent awareness of the symbolism of human systems&quot; exist on opposite ends of the point at which humans start having symbolism and unique systems. Beasts are notably the first splat since 1e changelings to not have some linguistic quirk as part of their template, whereas demons get the most broadly-applicable and immediately-usable such quality.<br /> <br /> You can have the Begotten in a world without wilderness without bringing back the wilderness, but the God-Machine both heavily uses and has been developing the current state of humanity as creatures of artifice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The &quot;Unnatural vs Natural&quot; argument breaks down when you look at 1. if it supported that either side is more &quot;natural&quot; than the other, and 2. why is the G-M the exception when Prometheans are obviously created, Arisen were created, and Deviants are created? </div> </div> </div>Prometheans are created by being infused with an entropic force that occasionally makes material agents without direct human intervention and the Arisen are the result of world-altering necromantic ritual. The Machine is a dispassionate Unmoved Mover that acts to preserve the state of the universe in those instances where it's not attempting to set up an occult matrix.<br /> <br /> Also, nobody said &quot;unnatural.&quot; The un-things of the Abyss can claim Kinship with the Children of the Dark Mother, but as pseudo-symbolic entities from a mad place outside of time wearing forms that loosely correspond to their true nature they can't rightly be called &quot;artificial.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm honestly curious how Beasts can claim Kinship to everything under the sun and moon <i>except</i>, strangely, anything G-M related. Where is the unifying element that is absent there? </div> </div> </div>In all probability it's the whole &quot;entropy&quot; thing \u2014 lack of Kinship doesn't stop Family Resemblance from potentially getting through Cover, and angels don't have that vulnerability.<br /> <br /> There's a few straightforward explanations that most readily come to mind for why the Machine isn't Kin:<br /> <br /> 1. Its arrival in the cosmology is later than whatever spawned the rest of the metaphysical frameworks and/from the Dark Mother.<br /> <br /> 2. It precedes and/or created the Dark Mother in a fashion that excised or never held a sympathetic connection to It.<br /> <br /> 3. It's the product of a massive-scale supernatural quality like the anti-Kinship the Leviathans of Vancouver exploit.<br /> <br /> 4. It is not supernatural in origin at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T09:58:50-07:00","id":876753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873215-beasts-and-the-god-machine?p=876730#post876730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;The animal parts of the collective human consciousness&quot; and &quot;the emergent awareness of the symbolism of human systems&quot; exist on opposite ends of the point at which humans start having symbolism and unique systems.</div> </div> </div> </div>This^<br /> <br /> Really this is the reason for me. Any other reason is just further explanation for this. The God-machine is the opposite of Primordial, its the culmination of complexity rather than base instinct. And this is important because it re-enforces the themes of BOTH game lines. And that is just awesome.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T10:04:42-07:00","id":876759,"title":"","content":"Maybe my thinking is to straightforward but the way i see it is this.<br /> The God-Machine doesn't want its agents to form kinship with Beasts (divided loyalties and all that) so they can't. As for the demons, the kinship would work adversarily with the cover i think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T11:10:59-07:00","id":876795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873215-beasts-and-the-god-machine?p=876759#post876759\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe my thinking is to straightforward but the way i see it is this.<br /> The God-Machine doesn't want its agents to form kinship with Beasts (divided loyalties and all that) so they can't. As for the demons, the kinship would work adversarily with the cover i think.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's my headcanon. Somewhere there's a piece of Infrastructure cutting Angels and Demons off from the Kinship of Beats, and their connection probably wasn't all that strong in the first place, due to the stuff that ElvesofZion and Satchel have been saying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T11:33:57-07:00","id":876818,"title":"","content":"Thematically Beasts and the God Machine are two different types of horror.<br /> <br /> Beasts are anthropocentric. They exist because of humanity's collective fears and live off causing humanity to feel fear. Humanity may be their prey but in a way it shows how immensely important humans are. They are something &quot;special&quot; that causes monsters to come knocking at their doors.<br /> <br /> The God Machine on the other hand is the Lovecraftian cosmic horror that inspires fear precisely because it shows humanity how unimportant and insignificant they are. The God Machine doesn't care about humanity other than for its usefulness, but the same could be said about G-M's views towards other resources like metal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11689-kokiteno","name":"Kokiteno","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T14:16:44-07:00","id":876964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873215-beasts-and-the-god-machine?p=876180#post876180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except, the metaphor was based on broken logic...</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Bx2wsi9.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/HgyL5oC.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/0fm5niS.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-28T14:26:41-07:00","id":876973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873215-beasts-and-the-god-machine?p=876964#post876964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Bx2wsi9.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/HgyL5oC.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/0fm5niS.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>Win. Win. You have done everything right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T03:54:28-07:00","id":877534,"title":"","content":"Do the Unchained (or the God-Machine itself) dream? Or otherwise have a subconscious? Building on <b>Xenorath</b>'s idea (not kin due to a lack of connection to the Astral) - if Beasts build their Kinship bonds through mutual ties to the Primordial Dream/collective subconscious, that could be the explanation. Vampires, werewolves, mages . . . heck, even the horrors of the Abyss dream (as the Fangs of Mara can testify). But if Demons don't . . . it'd be like someone on Wi-Fi trying to reach an un-networked printer. The connection just isn't there to transfer data/power/kinship through.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Solaris</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873215-beasts-and-the-god-machine?p=874085#post874085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What page in the Corebook is this? I have it and now I want to see it!</div> </div> </div> </div>Page 67, under &quot;Family Secrets&quot;. I think this is the final version they went with:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beast corebook</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mr. Void steals the Hero\u2019s soul. Wendigo doesn\u2019t mind, though. He likes to watch skins change hands. He can learn so much as the demon\u2019s mask crumbles with his new, despicable obligations, and even more when tungsten angels come to drag him back into service.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-29T10:12:05-07:00","id":877846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873215-beasts-and-the-god-machine?p=877534#post877534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do the Unchained (or the God-Machine itself) dream? Or otherwise have a subconscious?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup.<br /> <br /> Take a look at the Nightmare Labyrinth in the Demon Storyteller's Guide. You may notice something familiar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T11:51:48-07:00","id":882063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873215-beasts-and-the-god-machine?p=876629#post876629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2) Nyx's point is made, if you read the whole of her point. Oil and Water might not have been the best icons, sure, but it gets the idea of what they're talking about across. as is often the point, it's the image and enough of the context that matters. I dunno what Jacob's whining about, because I can't read a thing he says, but I'm fairly sure it's a realm of minutia that's beyond the point you were to take away from the image and the initial context.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I thought the oil and water part worked perfectly. Beast and Demons are very much like oil and water. What doesn't work, which was my point, was the idea that Beasts are something &quot;natural&quot; and Demons are something &quot;artificial.&quot; Oils occur naturally too. But more to the point the machine imagery in Demon isn't really serving the purpose of drawing a distinction between what is natural and what is artificial. Demon is a allegory for the system that the universe seems to operate by. As such I interpret the machine imagery as serving as a metaphor for the <i>uncaringness</i> of that system (and certainly you're free to YMMV as you like). Wild animals and other <i>natural</i> things also have a certain <i>uncaringness</i>, especially with regard to human beings. Seen in this light, the natural/artificial portion of Nyx's mixed metaphor doesn't work because whether they're natural or artificial, neither Demons nor Beasts care overly much about human beings. This is a property they share in common, regardless of their supernatural origin or the imagery used.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-04T12:28:59-07:00","id":882087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873215-beasts-and-the-god-machine?p=882063#post882063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Seen in this light, the natural/artificial portion of Nyx's mixed metaphor doesn't work because whether they're natural or artificial, neither Demons nor Beasts care overly much about human beings. This is a property they share in common, regardless of their supernatural origin or the imagery used.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, for me, in this light I'd say the opposite. I agree that Demons represent the natural in this sense, but say that Beasts, being the embodiement of human fears, actually represent the artifical. Also, they do care about humans, in that the feed on them, (maybe) used to be one (at least lived as one for a good while) and for some at least want to teach them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T09:00:40-07:00","id":884665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873215-beasts-and-the-god-machine?p=882087#post882087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, for me, in this light I'd say the opposite. I agree that Demons represent the natural in this sense, but say that Beasts, being the embodiement of human fears, actually represent the artifical. Also, they do care about humans, in that the feed on them, (maybe) used to be one (at least lived as one for a good while) and for some at least want to teach them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I don't get a sense that the bobcat chewing off my arm cares about me any more than the bandsaw chewing off my arm does but YMMV. Beasts are monsters after all. I think the whole wisdom thing is overwrought and whether or not Beasts themselves represent human-made fears, Beasts must feed!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-07T11:14:43-07:00","id":884762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873215-beasts-and-the-god-machine?p=884665#post884665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally I don't get a sense that the bobcat chewing off my arm cares about me any more than the bandsaw chewing off my arm does but YMMV. Beasts are monsters after all. I think the whole wisdom thing is overwrought and whether or not Beasts themselves represent human-made fears, Beasts must feed!</div> </div> </div> </div>Demons are capable of emotion, that's why they fell. They choose to display them, tho. Hell, they're more capable of, if not morality, ethics than your average Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T14:01:24-07:00","id":885673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873215-beasts-and-the-god-machine?p=884762#post884762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Demons are capable of emotion, that's why they fell. They choose to display them, tho. Hell, they're more capable of, if not morality, ethics than your average Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uncaring and being incapable of emotion are two different things.<br /> <br /> Regarding morality and ethics...really? That seems to overplay the alienness of Beasts while over identifying the Demonic condition with the human one.<br /> <br /> Do Demons have morailty and ethics? Sure. But these don't necessarily resemble human conceptions of these things. And I don't see Beasts as being any different than Demons in this respect; Beasts are no less capable of having morality and ethics. And like Demonic morality and ethics, it's no less inscrutable from a human perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-08T19:34:38-07:00","id":885895,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/873215-beasts-and-the-god-machine?p=877846#post877846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yup.<br /> <br /> Take a look at the Nightmare Labyrinth in the Demon Storyteller's Guide. You may notice something familiar.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I don't have <b>Demon</b>. Hence my question <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-09T07:18:43-07:00","id":886209,"title":"","content":"For me, the answer to the original question is spelled out on page 170 of Chronicles of Darkness corebook (dunno which page it is in the previous GMC book):<br /> <br /> <b>&quot;No human mythology ever conceived of a god so alien to the mortal mind.&quot;</b><br /> <br /> Monsters have fired up human imagination pretty much ever since the dawn of our species. For as long as we've existed, we've been making offerings to placate the hungry dead, praying to gods, spirits and demons for protection or mercy, avoiding the magical groves where the Fair Folk might dwell, looking up to the priests, magi and assorted mystics wielding supernatural powers.<br /> <br /> Chronicles of Darkness is a game where all these ancient fears have actual basis in reality, even if the stories passed may get a ton of details wrong. Gods (spirits) exist, so do the hungry dead of both material and immaterial variety. Mad Fae can indeed abduct you, you can become a target of a werewolf hunt, get caught up in the intrigues of mages or chance upon pretty much any other creature from assorted mythologies, folktales and legends.<br /> <br /> Then, there's the God-Machine, a being with no semblance to any known horrors of yore. Maybe it's because it didn't exist until recently. Maybe it's simply been more careful, better hidden than the other monsters lurking in the dark. Maybe it's because just a couple decades ago, our knowledge of the universe was too unrefined to comprehend the terror of the God-Machine, even if we could glimpse it. Whatever the reason, God-Machine simply isn't something our ancestors feared, had nightmares and told cautionary tales about, and as such, isn't a part of the Primordial Dream either.<br /> <br /> Maybe it'll change over time. Computers dictating the course of our lives are a modern fear, but one that gradually gains basis in reality (just ask anyone who got screwed over by a credit history he didn't even know he had). Conspiracy theories and stories about weird things found in the deep web are quickly becoming the modern folktales. Maybe over time enough knowledge of the God-Machine will trickle down into our species' memory that he, too, will become part of the Primordial Dream, and the Begotten of the future will welcome his angels and demons as kin thanks to that.<br /> <br /> Then again, maybe it's just the God-Machine's nature is so fundamentally different, it'll never be able to tickle our lizard brain the same way a vampire or werewolf does.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}